I started playing this game about 15 (?) years ago on networked Unix
computers at Uni.  It was around about the time when one of my mates
told me that he could use his student computer-mail-address (can't
remember if the term 'e-mail' was around then) to contact his
brother in Norway.

So, about my game: I messed up Sokoban and didn't have a WoTeleport
to fix it, but I think I already had a BoH and reflection by the time I
came I ventured that way.  I went back later but messed up another
level so never completed Sokoban.

I keep bones files, got lucky this game as I encountered 2 ghosts
relatively early, and another on the level with all the water.  However
this made me mess around on that water level more than I normally
would, so I ended up falling in the water about 5 times (idiot!)  Not a
good idea to dig next to a lake too hmmmmm.  Lost a lot of scrolls and
spellbooks, but did pick up a few useful items, including 3 'stoning
grenades'.

Anyway this game was played over about 2 or 3 months, I'd never seen
"Rodney" before so I let myself get pretty spoilt towards the end
as I just couldn't bear yet another choking/stoning/death ray or
other YASD.  Couldn't resist playing on the recent Friday 13th all
the same...

I did a little bit of polypiling and nurse-dancing, but didn't
'savescum'.  I avoiding using the rubber chicken as it's given me
too many YASDs in the past, but I did use a grenade to stone Rodney
thinking that I might be able to kill him for good, I stoned him over
water after he'd stolen my Mitre of Holiness.  Had to get underwater
to try to get the Mitre back but it seemed it was gone for good.

I'd carried a BoH full of goodies all the way to the Astral Plane but
dropped it as soon as I got there.  Had a much better AC before, think
I did something to lose all the protection I'd bought.  Finished the
game carrying some spare goodies like another AoLS, magic lamp, scoll
of charging, WoDeaths, unicorn horn, more BoHs etc.  But that also
meant that I finished with no gold, gems etc, I didn't want to risk
going back, especially seeing that the Chaotic alter was the third one
I visited.  Basically just used WoDeath and WoTeleport to get through
to the right alter to win the game.

Ahhhhhh so now I've made it through Nethack.  Hopefully I've kicked
the addiction    ;O)

